{"name":"Tretinoin + microneedling stack","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["This stack combines prescription tretinoin, a topical retinoid, with microneedling, often at home with a derma roller, to smooth acne scars and texture and to soften signs of aging.","Tretinoin speeds cell turnover and acts on collagen over weeks to months, and it is described as the most extensively studied retinoid for photoaging. Microneedling makes controlled punctures intended to stimulate repair and has been used for scarring and acne. No trial of the two together was found."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["Users run the two as a long-term routine, with tretinoin applied on a regular schedule and microneedling sessions spaced out, with changes usually appearing over months. Many people pause the retinoid around needling sessions."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Tretinoin commonly causes irritation, dryness and sun sensitivity and is prescription-only in many countries. Microneedling carries infection concerns when done without proper hygiene."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Efficacy of Botulinum Toxin A for the Management of Melasma: A Split-Face, Randomized Control Study.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40747795/","source":"Journal of cosmetic dermatology","year":2025,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"Guidelines of care for the management of acne vulgaris.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38300170/","source":"Journal of the American Academy of Dermatology","year":2024,"cites":null,"kind":"Systematic Review"},{"title":"Management of androgenic alopecia: a systematic review of the literature.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38852607/","source":"Journal of cosmetic and laser therapy : official publication of the European Society for Laser Dermatology","year":2024,"cites":null,"kind":"Systematic Review"},{"title":"Chemical Peels in Treatment of Melasma.","u