tene for anti aging","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin-versus-tazarotene-for-anti-aging.473102/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220517022040/https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin-versus-tazarotene-for-anti-aging.473102/"},{"title":"tretinoin source in the us","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin-source-in-the-us.424244/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220121173339/https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin-source-in-the-us.424244/"},{"title":"tretinoin","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin.423435/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211203095800/https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin.423435/"},{"title":"tretinoin fucked me","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin-fucked-me.334909/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210721020209/https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin-fucked-me.334909/"},{"title":"tretinoin gel is 0 1 too strong","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin-gel-is-0-1-too-strong.10532/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250710173002/https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin-gel-is-0-1-too-strong.10532/"},{"title":"whats the difference between retinol and tretinoin","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/whats-the-difference-between-retinol-and-tretinoin.2261297/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260815020716/https://looksmax.org/threads/whats-the-difference-between-retinol-and-tretinoin.2261297/"},{"title":"accutane tretinoin","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/accutane-tretinoin.1783633/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251229142849/https://looksmax.org/threads/accutane-tretinoin.1783633/"}],"news":[],"social":[{"title":"If I wait for my face to be completely dry before applying tretinoin (which is recommended practice afaik) my moisturizer (which is recommended to be applied on damp skin) will not be able to trap muc","url":"https://kbin.social/m/skincareaddiction@sh.itjust.works/p/895519","site":"Lemmy · skincareaddiction","score":10,"comments":4,"year":2023}],"web":[{"title":"Tretinoin - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tretinoin"},{"title":"Microneedling - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microneedling"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Skin","chain":["Retinoid speeds cell turnover","Microneedling stimulates collagen","Smoother scars and texture"],"effect":"indirect","text":"Appearance forums pair prescription tretinoin, which speeds cell turnover and builds collagen, with microneedling, which triggers repair, for smoother scars and texture. Each part has its own research, and the combination has not been studied."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["The tretinoin plus microneedling stack is a skin-care protocol discussed in appearance forums that combines a topical retinoid (tretinoin) with microneedling, typically with a derma roller, aiming at acne scars, texture and aging signs.","Each component has its own literature. Topical tretinoin is described as the most extensively studied retinoid for photoaging, with improvement usually taking weeks to months, and irritation is its main adverse effect [1]. Microneedling has been used for scarring and acne [2]. Neither reference describes the two as a combined protocol, and no trial of the combination was identified for this article."],"infobox":[["Type","Combined topical and procedural protocol"],["Components","Tretinoin; microneedling"],["Tretinoin status","Prescription-only in US, UK, EU and Australia"],["Combination evidence","None identified"]],"sections":[{"h":"Components","paras":["Tretinoin is a retinoid used for comedonal and inflammatory acne and photoaging. It was approved by the FDA for acne in 1971 and is prescription-only in several countries [1]. Common adverse effects of the topical form are redness, swelling and irritation, and increased sun sensitivity [1].","Microneedling, also called collagen induction therapy, repeatedly punctures the skin with sterile needles. It has been used for scarring and acne, and research on combinations such as platelet-rich plasma is described as ongoing [2]. Health officials have warned about infection risks when related services are performed without infection-control training [2]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"The stack in practice","paras":["Forum users describe using tretinoin on a nightly schedule and microneedling at intervals, with the belief that the two reinforce collagen stimulation. Protocol details were not drawn from the sources reviewed and are not given here. Dermatology references on each component do not address how they interact, and skin irritation from both together has not been characterized in the sources reviewed."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1971","event":"Tretinoin approved by the FDA for acne [1]."}],"refs":[{"title":"Tretinoin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tretinoin","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Microneedling","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microneedling","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"tretinoin fucked me up need advice","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin-fucked-me-up-need-advice.1809105/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260204225325/https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin-fucked-me-up-need-advice.1809105/"},{"title":"Tretinoin source","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin-source.1760036/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251221213741/https://looksmax.org/threads/tretinoin-source.1760036/"},{"title":"Derma roller on eyebrows?","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/derma-roller-on-eyebrows.1758611/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251219141339/https://looksmax.org/threads/derma-roll